From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] OWE: Skip HT beacon updates with MTK AP SME

MTK AP SME manages HT operation and beacon generation during OWE
association. A beacon update from hostapd also runs driver AP security
initialization, including group key index initialization.

OWE association processing retains hostapd's HT station accounting but
does not request a beacon update for that HT state change when MTK AP
SME is in use. Beacon updates requested for other changes remain enabled.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -6090,7 +6090,13 @@ static void handle_assoc(struct hostapd_
 			set_beacon = true;
 	}
 
+#if defined(CONFIG_OWE) && defined(CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_MTK)
+	if (update_ht_state(hapd, sta) > 0 &&
+	    (!(hapd->iface->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_MTK_AP_SME) ||
+	     wpa_auth_sta_key_mgmt(sta->wpa_sm) != WPA_KEY_MGMT_OWE))
+#else /* CONFIG_OWE && CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_MTK */
 	if (update_ht_state(hapd, sta) > 0)
+#endif /* CONFIG_OWE && CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_MTK */
 		set_beacon = true;
 
 	hostapd_logger(hapd, sta->addr, HOSTAPD_MODULE_IEEE80211,
